[{"id":3033379725,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc60zbON","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","login":"dsnopek","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108737#pullrequestreview-3033379725","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108737","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-07-18T12:28:36Z"},{"id":3045163893,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc61gYN1","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally on Linux host + Samsung Galaxy S25 Ultra target, it works as expected. Code looks good to me.\r\n\r\nThis is pretty nice, as you can do other things on the Android device while it's running. It also lets you test resolutions/aspect ratios not supported by the target device (without needing to use `adb` shell commands to forcibly change the display resolution). Additionally, it makes it easy to use hardware keyboard input for testing. Gamepad input should also be able to work according to scrcpy's changelog, but I didn't test it.\r\n\r\n![android_scrcpy_superwide webp](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7f7450f1-7095-4beb-855d-baf6fc2329ad)\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- `scrcpy` from the system `PATH` is detected automatically, so no configuration is needed in this case.\r\n\r\n```\r\nscrcpy 3.2 <https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy>\r\n\r\nDependencies (compiled / linked):\r\n - SDL: 2.32.2 / 2.32.2\r\n - libavcodec: 61.19.101 / 61.19.101\r\n - libavformat: 61.7.100 / 61.7.100\r\n - libavutil: 59.39.100 / 59.39.100\r\n - libavdevice: 61.3.100 / 61.3.100\r\n - libusb: - / 1.0.28\r\n```\r\n\r\n- The virtual display seems to be limited to 60 Hz, even on a 120 Hz device that will stream at 120 FPS when not using the virtual display option. This will limit the reported FPS to 60 since V-Sync will cap the framerate. Is there a way to change the virtual display's refresh rate? I made sure to disable power saving options, including the one in developer settings that caps certain games to 60 FPS.\r\n\r\n- The audio volume you hear on your PC is dependent on the target device's audio volume, so turn it up on the device if you can't hear anything. It will work even when using the virtual display, and even when the device is locked. The device itself won't mirror the audio, effectively making your PC act as headphones (or speakers). Double-check Do Not Disturb status as well (if you've configured it to block media playback).\r\n\r\n- System performance will be lower when the device is locked (or has its screen turned off in general), which can lead to dropped frames and higher latency. This is important, as Keep Screen On won't have an effect on the actual device when using a virtual device. This means the target device will eventually lock itself after some inactivity, even if you are currently playing the game on the PC.\r\n\r\n  - I wish scrcpy indicated this in the window title when the device is locked, but this should be an improvement made at the scrcpy level.\r\n\r\n- An `Ime` -> `IME` conversion should be added to EditorPropertyNameProcessor (for the new editor setting).\r\n\r\nFurther things to research:\r\n\r\n- See if higher-quality video encoding options can be used on modern Android devices, as the default doesn't look great if you have significant amounts of texture detail, especially at high resolutions. I recall playing around with this in 2023 and finding some good options, but I unfortunately didn't take notes.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108737#pullrequestreview-3045163893","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108737","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-07-22T23:50:16Z"},{"id":3080882173,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc63oof9","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?u=5f2b0cb28e37393252e96695f2eaa33494930285&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","login":"m4gr3d","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108737#pullrequestreview-3080882173","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108737","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-08-02T03:06:43Z"},{"id":3082371776,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc63uULA","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?u=74caa4e396a8e2995ac648a80f7488601d679e63&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","login":"Alex2782","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782"},"bod